# Ordered structure of interlayer constructed with metal-organic frameworks improves the performance of lithium-sulfur batteries

Sijia Guo\(^{1,\S}\), Yingbo Xiao\(^{1,\S}\), Jia Wang\(^{1}\), Yuan Ouyang\(^{1}\), Xin Li\(^{1}\), Haoyan Deng\(^{1}\), Wenchao He\(^{1}\), Qinghan Zeng\(^{1}\), Wei Zhang\(^{1}\), Qi Zhang\(^{1,2}\) (✉), and Shaoming Huang\(^{1,2}\) (✉)

\(^{1}\) Guangzhou Key Laboratory of Low-Dimensional Materials and Energy Storage Devices, School of Materials and Energy, Guangdong University of Technology, Guangzhou 510006, China  \(^{2}\) Synergy Innovation Institute of GDUT, Heyuan 517000, China  \(^{3}\) Sijia Guo and Yingbo Xiao contributed equally to this work.

